                                        "entry_id": "29c07e9a-d349-35b3-91ba-fd85f35ae381",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In bad faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33084b20-9912-4701-a278-2271f9a10616",
                                                "sense_id": "99062dfb-fab8-3476-ac0b-bcf579a03028",
                                                "text": "Having regard to this dictum it is clear to me that the plaintiff cannot rely on negotiorum gestorum to recover damages. The gestor, ie the plaintiff, did not intend to serve the dominus, ie the defendants. The gestor did not act bona fide in the mistaken belief that he was serving the dominus. It was the plaintiff's evidence that in an attempt to preserve its good name and reputation it was decided to accept the cancellation of the agreement. It is thus clear that the gestor, the plaintiff acted mala fide in its own interest. In my view, the plaintiff cannot succeed on this principle of negotiorum gestorum."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
